<Project>

  <!--
    Solution-wide C# defaults for the Volt toolchain.

    These were hand-copied into all eleven csprojs. `Nullable` and `LangVersion` happened to agree; ImplicitUsings
    did NOT — four projects enabled it, two disabled it, and five said nothing (which means disabled). That is not
    a decision anyone made, it is drift, and every new project inherited a coin flip.

    Settled on ImplicitUsings=enable: the two largest projects (Volt.Engine, Volt.Cli) already relied on it, and it
    is the SDK default for new work. Projects that were previously off simply gain the implicit set; nothing is
    taken away. A project needing the old behaviour overrides it locally and says why.

    NOT set here, deliberately:
      - TargetFramework. It is load-bearing and different per project — net48 for the in-process CODESYS bridge,
        net8.0-windows for the TwinCAT worker and the tray, netstandard2.0 for everything both must share. A
        default would only ever be wrong somewhere and would hide the one constraint that shapes the whole tree.
      - TreatWarningsAsErrors. Turning it on today FAILS the build: Volt.Engine ships five CS8604 warnings
        (PouDocument and four sites in PushService), all on the push path. They want fixing on their own merits,
        not as collateral of a build-settings change. Enable this once they are gone.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
